cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this repository or its results are used, please cite it as below."
title: "The Great Rewiring: Pricing Modern Mercantilism and Artificial Intelligence on the World Trade Web"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction package for a study that treats the world trade network as a single object and
  prices two simultaneous resource grabs against it. It ports the CompleNet 2022 synthetic
  world-trade-web generator to Python, validates the port against the published statistics to
  within approximately 2.9%, runs it forward as a no-rewiring null, tests that null with a
  uniformity placebo across roughly 2,653 comparable dyads, finds it approximately 4.1 times
  over-confident, and replaces it with an Efron empirical null. Also contains an attack
  percolation of the 2024 network and ten locked binary forecasts.
